mh2lm: diagnose PM8150B charging policy gates (0124)

The status bar and the existing `SWEET BATT DIAG` prove physical VBUS
presence, but they do not show whether the PM8150B SMB5 input path has the
Type-C, APSD and AICL prerequisites that Linux configures before it releases
the default charge-disable vote.  In particular, state 7 and an unset
CHARGING_ENABLE_CMD bit alone do not say whether a future controller must
first configure the input policy or whether it is only disabled by policy.

Add a `SWEET BATT POLICY` diagnostic line under the existing opt-in
`sweetbattdiag=1` guard.  It reads (and never writes) the SMB5 power path,
USB input suspend/current/AICL controls, APSD status, Type-C sink/state/misc
status, and SMB_EN control/select bytes.  The decoded fields use the MH2LM
Lineage SMB5 definitions: 50 mA per PM8150B ICL code, Type-C state-attach
bit 5, CC-attach bit 0, VBUS bit 5, and AICL enable/ADC/rerun/collapse bits.

Also correct 0123's cosmetic IRQ diagnostic string: it emitted a literal
`\\n` instead of ending the record.  No interrupt enable, latch clear,
charger configuration or charger command is added by this patch.

